std: child processes on WebAssembly Linux (tombl/linux) without fork. The kernel cannot copy the
memory of a process that has more than one thread, so the fork path of Command::spawn (taken for
pre_exec closures, as the jobserver crate's, a changed PATH, setsid, uid/gid, ...) fails there. The
child runs instead as posix_spawn's does: clone(CLONE_VM | CLONE_VFORK) on a stack of its own, in the
parent's memory, the parent waiting until it has exec'd or exited; so it must not change the
parent's globals (environ: execve with the environment, PATH searched in it; no always_abort).

